MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Turtles and Beach Boys feel like natural next choices because their melodic '60s pop and vocal harmonies connect closely with my AM Gold and other older pop collections.",
    "Seals & Crofts and Gordon Lightfoot fit the gentle acoustic sound and storytelling I enjoy in Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and Queen connect with my classic rock listening, but they are less compelling right now because I am leaning toward gentler folk-pop and harmonies.",
    "I cannot judge the album titled Greatest Hits without knowing the artist; the title alone gives me no reason to expect music I would enjoy."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "I enjoy many greatest-hits collections, but that format alone does not make a collection appealing; the artist and sound matter more.",
    "My classic rock listening seems to have been treated as a broad preference, even though some of those choices fit my current mood much less closely than acoustic songs and melodic pop."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my Melanie, Jonathan Edwards, and Simon & Garfunkel listening deserves more weight because gentle voices and acoustic storytelling are especially appealing to me now.",
    "Several albums suit my overall taste without being something I would choose today; I would save Carpenters and Carly Simon while prioritizing the strongest matches to my current mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in older pop and familiar collections, but only some captured the gentle harmonies and acoustic storytelling I want right now."
}
